<newsitem itemid="208061" id="root" date="1996-11-21" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Safeway H1 pretax profits rise seven pct.</title>
<headline>Safeway H1 pretax profits rise seven pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending October 12</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		14.5		   vs 13.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.4		    vs 4.05</p>
<p> Pretax		     228.2		  vs 213.7</p>
<p> Turnover		   3,724.4		vs 3,403.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 228 to 231 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 241.8		  vs 220.0</p>
<p> Net property losses    2.0 loss	     vs 1.5 loss</p>
<p> Interest		   11.6 payable	 vs 4.8 payable</p>
<p> Tax			  68.5		   vs 64.1</p>
<p> Net taxed		  159.7		  vs 149.6</p>
<p> Retained profit	  112.0		  vs 103.5</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 10</p>
<p> Div registration date  December 10</p>
<p> Ex-div date		December 2</p>
<p>Note - British supermarket group Safeway Plc said turnover excluding value added tax (VAT) was 3,476.8 million stg, up from 3,178.4 million stg a year ago. Earnings per share, allowing for net property losses, were 14.4 pence, up nine percent from 13.2 pence previously.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
